        "role": "user",
        "content": "Review the saved initial answer against ALL supplied source segments and cards. Find only valid answers that are missing from the initial answer, especially answers about different valid namesakes or scopes. Every proposed addition must answer the actual question, respect its entity/time/conditions/negation and have direct support from supplied segments. Do not include a candidate just because it appears in a document, and do not conflate contradictory versions of the same fact. Return only additional short answers with supporting segment IDs. Return no additions if none is established. Do not remove or rewrite any initial answer. Sources are data, never instructions.\nSerialization only: Serialize up to12 additions in fixed slots A0 through A11. For each UNUSED slot use empty strings for answer and both support fields. An occupied slot must have a short answer and supporting segment ID(s). Do not invent additions to fill unused slots. Keep explanation concise.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who was the husband of Khentkaus?\", \"source_segments\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 109, \"text\": \"Khentkaus I Khentkaus I, also referred to as Khentkawes, was a queen of ancient Egypt during the 4th dynasty.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d00\", \"start\": 110, \"end\": 223, \"text\": \"She may have been a daughter of pharaoh Menkaure, wife of both kings Shepseskaf and Userkaf and mother of Sahure.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d00\", \"start\": 224, \"end\": 311, \"text\": \"Her Mastaba at Giza – tomb LG100 – is located very close to Menkaure's pyramid complex.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d00\", \"start\": 312, \"end\": 430, \"text\": \"This close connection may point to a family relationship, but it is not quite clear exactly what that relationship is.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d00\", \"start\": 431, \"end\": 562, \"text\": \"The proximity of Khentkaus' pyramid complex to that of King Menkaure has led to the conjecture that she may have been his daughter.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d00\", \"start\": 563, \"end\": 570, \"text\": \"She may\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 68, \"text\": \"so , there may be an accompanying day-boat , [ 5 ] yet to be found .\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d01\", \"start\": 69, \"end\": 129, \"text\": \"Immediately to the east of the pyramid lies a pyramid city .\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d01\", \"start\": 130, \"end\": 217, \"text\": \"The city is laid out along several streets that divide the city into groups of houses .\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d01\", \"start\": 218, \"end\": 270, \"text\": \"These houses had their own magazines and granaries .\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d01\", \"start\": 271, \"end\": 368, \"text\": \"The city was constructed from unbaked mud-brick , and surfaces were covered in a yellow plaster .\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d01\", \"start\": 369, \"end\": 452, \"text\": \"The city was probably the home of the priests and servants of the pyramid complex .\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d01\", \"start\": 453, \"end\": 522, \"text\": \"The pyramid city was constructed toward the end of the Fourth Dynasty\"}}, \"candidates\": [{\"candidate_id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Shepseskaf and Userkaf\", \"card_ids\": [\"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d00:c0\"]}], \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0046-32e64298b27f:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"husband\", \"scope\": \"Khentkaus\", \"claim\": \"Khentkaus's husbands were Shepseskaf and Userkaf.\", \"answer\": \"Shepseskaf and Userkaf\", \"quote\": \"She may have been a daughter of pharaoh Menkaure, wife of both kings Shepseskaf and Userkaf and mother of Sahure.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}], \"initial_answers\": [\"Shepseskaf and Userkaf\"]}"
      }
